    {
      "note": "Corrected: *again* adds a repetition the Hebrew does not write beside a verb whose lexeme *restore* has already written, so no morpheme licenses it and it is its own `added` unit, exactly as rule 44 leaves the *back* of `בּוֹא` hiphil → *bring him back*. It is not folded into the verb, the object or the adverb standing beside it, for the reason rule 42 gives about a surplus *and*. The competing reading, taken in the accepted alignment, kept *restore … again* whole as one rendering; JDG.11.8's *turned again* and JDG.11.9's *bring home again* are the other side of the same test, where the bare English verb does not write the returning.",
